{"`rescue nil` catches all exceptions broadly, which can hide unexpected runtime errors and make debugging harder. Should rescue `URI::InvalidURIError` explicitly or use a safe URL parser helper to handle malformed URLs intentionally while keeping the failure mode clear.": 0.7725706696510315, "The subdomain comparison logic `website_host.split('.')[1..-1].join('.') == discourse_host.split('.')[1..-1].join('.')` only strips one subdomain level, which can misclassify deeper subdomain structures. For example, if website is `a.b.example.com` and instance is `forum.example.com`, this will incorrectly compare `b.example.com` vs `example.com`. Should use a more robust domain parsing approach (e.g., eTLD+1 aware library or shared utility) to reliably compare registrable domains.": 0.735284149646759}